WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:19.551
"What?" Anna cried as everyone else gasped.

2
00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:24.231
"Why do you think Anna stole the tickets, Henry?" Nathan asked.

3
00:00:24.232 --> 00:00:29.305
"She's the only one with the motive and the opportunity," Henry said.

4
00:00:29.306 --> 00:00:33.848
"She's been saving to buy a game player, so we know she needed money.

5
00:00:33.849 --> 00:00:40.202
When she got to that tide pool first, she decided to go grab the booty for herself."

6
00:00:40.203 --> 00:00:44.192
William turned to Anna. "Is that true?"

7
00:00:44.193 --> 00:00:49.754
Anna's shoulders slumped. "I didn't mean to do it! It was an accident."

8
00:00:49.755 --> 00:00:54.669
Maggie scowled. "How can you steal something by accident?"

9
00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.479
"Yeah!" chimed in Luke.

10
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:05.372
Anna sighed. "I was about to check one tide pool when I realized that another one is shaped like a teardrop.

11
00:01:05.373 --> 00:01:12.872
Just like the clue!" Anna went on. "So I got excited and ran to that one."

12
00:01:12.873 --> 00:01:17.345
"That must be when Roger saw you running on the beach," Cole said.

13
00:01:17.346 --> 00:01:22.206
"When I got to the tide pool, nobody else was there yet," Anna went on.

14
00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:25.128
"I spotted the box in the water and grabbed it.

15
00:01:25.129 --> 00:01:28.348
I thought the envelope had money inside."

16
00:01:28.349 --> 00:01:31.764
"So you decided to steal it?" Maggie demanded.

17
00:01:31.765 --> 00:01:35.449
"I was thinking about taking some of it," Anna admitted.

18
00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:41.450
"Enough to buy myself a game player. I had gum in my pocket," she went on.

19
00:01:41.451 --> 00:01:43.815
"So I dropped that in the box.

20
00:01:43.816 --> 00:01:47.460
I thought the gum might make up for taking some of the money."

21
00:01:47.461 --> 00:01:53.040
Tears filled her eyes. "I know it was wrong—really wrong."

22
00:01:53.041 --> 00:01:58.497
Luke was staring at her in disbelief. "I can't believe you stole our stuff!"

23
00:01:58.498 --> 00:02:00.199
Anna bit her lip.

24
00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:05.574
"Once I realized that the envelope didn't have money, I wanted to put it back in the box.

25
00:02:05.575 --> 00:02:10.778
But I heard someone coming. I panicked and stuck the envelope in my pocket.

26
00:02:10.779 --> 00:02:15.515
Then I tossed the box back in the water and sneaked away before anyone saw me."

27
00:02:15.516 --> 00:02:20.421
Nathan frowned at Anna. "How could you do something like that?"

28
00:02:20.422 --> 00:02:25.862
"I'm sorry." Tears rolled down Anna's cheeks.

29
00:02:25.863 --> 00:02:29.342
She pulled an envelope out of her pocket and gave it to Henry.

30
00:02:29.343 --> 00:02:32.327
"I never meant to ruin anyone's fun.

31
00:02:32.328 --> 00:02:36.216
I just wasn't thinking, and now I feel terrible.

32
00:02:36.217 --> 00:02:39.912
I don't even want a video game player anymore!"

33
00:02:39.913 --> 00:02:43.224
Henry couldn't help feeling a little sorry for Anna.

34
00:02:43.225 --> 00:02:46.630
"I made a terrible mistake," she went on.

35
00:02:46.631 --> 00:02:50.769
"And I owe your parents a big apology too, William."

36
00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:54.439
He nodded coolly. "You sure do, Anna."

37
00:02:54.440 --> 00:03:00.500
Looking miserable, Anna headed back to the beach house to apologize to William's parents.

38
00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:03.613
"Come on, you guys," Maggie said to the others.

39
00:03:03.614 --> 00:03:07.273
"We have one more treasure to find!"

40
00:03:07.274 --> 00:03:12.600
They all ran to the bandstand.

41
00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:16.035
A cooler with a skull and crossbones sat there.

42
00:03:16.036 --> 00:03:18.633
Henry read the note that was taped to it.

43
00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:24.057
"We're supposed to carry the cooler back to William's beach house," he informed his friends.

44
00:03:24.058 --> 00:03:29.978
"It will get filled up with something there."

45
00:03:29.979 --> 00:03:35.243
As they hurried back to William's house, The Lemonade Detectives talked about the case.

46
00:03:35.244 --> 00:03:40.038
"How did you figure out that Anna was the thief?" Maggie asked Henry.

47
00:03:40.039 --> 00:03:44.959
Henry shrugged. "It was the only answer that fit all the clues."

48
00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:48.725
"A few things still don't make sense though," Cole said.

49
00:03:48.726 --> 00:03:51.764
"Why was Nathan acting weird all day?"

50
00:03:51.765 --> 00:03:56.787
They looked at Nathan. "Ah-choo!" Nathan sneezed.

51
00:03:56.788 --> 00:04:01.694
Henry smiled. "Another case closed," he said.

52
00:04:01.695 --> 00:04:04.874
"Nathan caught his sister's cold and isn't feeling well.

53
00:04:04.875 --> 00:04:07.860
That's why he's grumpy today!"

54
00:04:07.861 --> 00:04:12.398
"Okay," Maggie said. "But I have another question.

55
00:04:12.399 --> 00:04:15.817
Why was Roger hanging around us all day?"

56
00:04:15.818 --> 00:04:20.561
They'd just come within view of the beach house. Henry pointed.

57
00:04:20.562 --> 00:04:23.933
"I think we just solved that mystery too."

58
00:04:23.934 --> 00:04:28.122
There was a party set up on the deck with pirate decorations!

59
00:04:28.123 --> 00:04:31.231
Roger stood there, dressed in a pirate costume.

60
00:04:31.232 --> 00:04:34.947
"Ahoy, mateys!" he called, waving.

61
00:04:34.948 --> 00:04:41.206
"Come and enjoy your final booty—it's a pirate party!"

62
00:04:41.207 --> 00:04:47.715
They brought the cooler over, and Roger immediately filled it with ice and soda for them.

63
00:04:47.716 --> 00:04:53.563
Henry could see Anna standing off to the side, talking with William's parents in low tones.

64
00:04:53.564 --> 00:04:56.130
Henry and Maggie were watching her.

65
00:04:56.131 --> 00:05:01.195
"Do you think Anna and William can still be friends?" asked Maggie softly.

66
00:05:01.196 --> 00:05:04.225
"I'm not sure," Henry replied.

67
00:05:04.226 --> 00:05:11.638
"Anna seems pretty sorry about what she did, but friends don't steal from friends."

68
00:05:11.639 --> 00:05:17.857
"And cousins don't steal from cousins," Maggie added, banging her cup gently against Henry's.

69
00:05:17.858 --> 00:05:22.848
"Your parents must have set up this party while we were in town," Cole said to William.

70
00:05:22.849 --> 00:05:27.912
William grinned as he looked around the deck. "It's pretty cool, actually."

71
00:05:27.913 --> 00:05:32.941
"That's why Roger went to the general store earlier," Henry chimed in.

72
00:05:32.942 --> 00:05:35.922
"Anna's parents also do catering, remember?

73
00:05:35.923 --> 00:05:38.785
Roger must have been picking up the food."

74
00:05:38.786 --> 00:05:47.166
Maggie laughed. "It's a good thing we solved all the mysteries," she said. "Otherwise—"

75
00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:51.161
Just then Roger Redbeard popped up from behind Maggie.

76
00:05:51.162 --> 00:06:03.775
"I would have made you walk the plank!" he finished. "Aargh!"
